{"type": "message", "id": "2e00623f", "parentId": "882452ae", "timestamp": "2026-04-12T12:42:20.733Z", "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "thinking", "thinking": "Ah, right, those tools aren't installed. Hmm. Wait, what else? Wait, the web_search earlier didn't get the right paper. Let's try a different query: \"Attribution IoU box plot cs paper 2020 image 7\". Wait, or \"median Attribution IoU lower than 0.7 least variability\". Let's try that.", "thinkingSignature": "reasoning_content"}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "call_i60skt5pd19y71sgw8b1iepv", "name": "web_search", "arguments": {"query": "median Attribution IoU lower than 0.7 least variability box plot", "count": 10}}], "api": "openai-completions", "provider": "volcengine", "model": "doubao-seed-2-0-mini-260215", "usage": {"input": 20739, "output": 206, "cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 0, "totalTokens": 20945, "cost": {"input": 0, "output": 0, "cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0}}, "stopReason": "toolUse", "timestamp": 1775997738431, "responseId": "0217759977380152748f57c5f4210b3bc611acce6828c7ab1ca01"}}
{"type": "message", "id": "96b28065", "parentId": "2e00623f", "timestamp": "2026-04-12T12:42:25.935Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_i60skt5pd19y71sgw8b1iepv", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"median Attribution IoU lower than 0.7 least variability box plot\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"tookMs\": 5200,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9812983838b8c397\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nInterquartile Range and Boxplots (2 of 3) – Concepts in Statistics\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9812983838b8c397\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://pressbooks.cuny.edu/conceptsinstatistics/chapter/interquartile-range-and-boxplots-2-of-3-concepts-in-statistics/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0b37b9104789972a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe IQR is a way to measure the variability about the median. Now we use the five-number summary to make a new type of graph, the boxplot. Boxplots are commonly used to summarize a distribution of a quantitative variable.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0b37b9104789972a\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"March 30, 2023\",\n      \"siteName\": \"pressbooks.cuny.edu\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"335b740d50d1b496\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2.4 Visualizing Data With Boxplots – Introduction to Statistics for Engineers\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"335b740d50d1b496\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://openoregon.pressbooks.pub/lbccstatsforengineers/chapter/box-plots/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2e18f06f4d4324d8\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNotice for the boys, the heights in the upper 50% of the data were more variable, while for the girls, the heights in the lower 50% were more variable. All of the boys are taller than 50% of the girls. ... Use the online imathAS boxplot tool to create box and whisker plots. Horizontal boxplot box begins at the smallest value and Q1, 1, until the Q3 and median, 5, no median line is designated, and has its lone whisker extending from the Q3 to the largest value, 7.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2e18f06f4d4324d8\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"openoregon.pressbooks.pub\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fa48a0a3f182ec8e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nBox Plot Explained with Examples - Statistics By Jim\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fa48a0a3f182ec8e\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://statisticsbyjim.com/graphs/box-plot/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"341a69325771107a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIn the plot below, Group 2 has more variability than Group 1 because it has a longer box and whiskers. Group 1 ranges from approximately 3 to 7 while Group 2 ranges from roughly 1.5 to 9 · Learn more about Measures of Variability. To determine whether a distribution is skewed in a box plot, look at where the median line falls within the box and whiskers.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"341a69325771107a\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"May 18, 2023\",\n      \"siteName\": \"statisticsbyjim.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2f0db1e2fbaa4554\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nBox Plots | Introduction to Statistics – Gravina\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2f0db1e2fbaa4554\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://courses.lumenlearning.com/suny-fmcc-introstats1/chapter/box-plots/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c63a13e1b6d0cc00\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTo graph a box plot the following data points must be calculated: the minimum value, the first quartile, the median, the third quartile, and the maximum value. Once the box plot is graphed, you can display and compare distributions of data. Use the online imathAS box plot tool to create box and whisker plots. ... OpenStax, Statistics, Box Plots. Provided by: OpenStax. Located at: http://cnx.org/contents/30189442-6998-4686-ac05-ed152b91b9de@17.34:13/Introductory_Statistics. License: CC BY: Attribution\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c63a13e1b6d0cc00\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"courses.lumenlearning.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d965c9e4d55d751b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nUsing Box Plots to Understand Variability and Outliers in Data\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d965c9e4d55d751b\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://sixsigmadsi.com/box-plots/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2d130bb510a61bc1\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nHere’s an example of a box plot displaying three groups (Group A, Group B, and Group C) with their respective values. The box plot visualizes the distribution of the data, highlighting the median, quartiles, and any potential outliers within each group.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2d130bb510a61bc1\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"January 2, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"sixsigmadsi.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6f961ede3af09691\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nInterpret the key results for Boxplot - Minitab - Support\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"6f961ede3af09691\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://support.minitab.com/en-us/minitab/help-and-how-to/graphs/boxplot/interpret-the-results/key-results/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b4852159b7a4fea5\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nExamine your boxplot to look at the center and spread of your data and comp