 regions of an image by analyzing the gradients flowing into the last convolutional layer of the CNN</strong>. By computing the gradient of the predicted class score concerning the feature maps ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5f0e4c4d3c2f857c\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"May 1, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.analyticsvidhya.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5e84397e98b1ff86\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nInvestigate Classification Decisions Using Gradient Attribution Techniques - MATLAB & Simulink\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5e84397e98b1ff86\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.mathworks.com/help/deeplearning/ug/investigate-classification-decisions-using-gradient-attribution-techniques.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"16ca81177fe1aa68\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nFor examples, see ... The gradient attribution methods explored in this example provide pixel-resolution maps that show which pixels are most important to the network&#x27;s classification. They <strong>compute the gradient of the class score with respect to the input pixels</strong>.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"16ca81177fe1aa68\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.mathworks.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3353ce3308064ae7\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAugmented Grad-CAM++: Super-Resolution Saliency Maps for Visual Interpretation of Deep Neural Network\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3353ce3308064ae7\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.mdpi.com/2079-9292/12/23/4846\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"cb51f70e8dc1a1fe\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTo generate the object-bounding ... Grad-CAM++. IoU, which stands for intersection over union, is <strong>a metric used to assess the performance of object detection models</strong>....\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"cb51f70e8dc1a1fe\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"November 30, 2023\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.mdpi.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e7213e7b099be505\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nDemystifying Convolutional Neural Networks using ScoreCam | Towards Data Science\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e7213e7b099be505\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://towardsdatascience.com/demystifying-convolutional-neural-networks-using-scorecam-344a0456c48e/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2418df3ac9cfd1c2\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThere are several techniques used to generate saliency maps and the most common in them is <strong>gradient-based visualization which backpropagates the partial derivative of the score on the target class concerning the input layer</strong>.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2418df3ac9cfd1c2\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"January 31, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"towardsdatascience.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fbec861e359dd620\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nr/MachineLearning on Reddit: [P] Adapting Class Activation Maps for Object Detection and Semantic Segmentation\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fbec861e359dd620\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.reddit.com/r/MachineLearning/comments/rs65ei/p_adapting_class_activation_maps_for_object/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"386f776113637c3b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nWe just compute heat maps (in a ... inside a bounding box. If we consider CAM or GradCAM for image classification, we use <strong>softmax scores</strong>....\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"386f776113637c3b\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"December 30, 2021\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.reddit.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\