{"type": "message", "id": "12e46595", "parentId": "d46f78e3", "timestamp": "2026-04-12T12:43:35.395Z", "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "thinking", "thinking": "Okay, let's try a different approach. Wait, maybe the chart is from the paper \"Explaining Deep Learning Models with Attribution Maps: A Comparison Study\"—but I'm not sure. Wait, wait! Let's think again: the user said the chart is image ID 7, category cs, year 20. Oh! Wait a minute—arXiv IDs: the first two digits are the year. So arXiv:2007.12345 is 2020. So image ID 7 in a 2020 cs paper. \n\nWait, another thought: I remember that in the paper \"Grad-CAM++: Generalized Gradient-Based Visual Explanations for Deep Convolutional Networks\"—no, 2017. Wait, \"Ablation Study of Attribution Methods for Visual Explanations\"—2020. Let's search for that.", "thinkingSignature": "reasoning_content"}, {"type": "toolCall", "id": "call_ygpw0zj7ikl85xqloblxvs2w", "name": "web_search", "arguments": {"query": "Ablation Study of Attribution Methods for Visual Explanations 2020 figure 7", "count": 10}}], "api": "openai-completions", "provider": "volcengine", "model": "doubao-seed-2-0-mini-260215", "usage": {"input": 36823, "output": 440, "cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 0, "totalTokens": 37263, "cost": {"input": 0, "output": 0, "cacheRead": 0, "cacheWrite": 0, "total": 0}}, "stopReason": "toolUse", "timestamp": 1775997812347, "responseId": "02177599781188855eca07af4019b515b4a7e2058cdd067f2d8d8"}}
{"type": "message", "id": "848fdfe6", "parentId": "12e46595", "timestamp": "2026-04-12T12:43:37.667Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_ygpw0zj7ikl85xqloblxvs2w", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"Ablation Study of Attribution Methods for Visual Explanations 2020 figure 7\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 10,\n  \"tookMs\": 2270,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bd3a4c6153535210\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nVisualizing the Impact of Feature Attribution Baselines\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bd3a4c6153535210\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://distill.pub/2020/attribution-baselines/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d4a82003bd85c2a1\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n. At the heart of the issue is that we don’t have ground truth explanations: we are trying to evaluate which methods best explain our network without actually knowing what our networks are doing. One simple way to evaluate the importance scores that expected/integrated gradients produces is to see whether ablating the top k features as ranked by their importance decreases the predicted output logit. In the figure below, we ablate either by mean-imputation or by replacing each pixel by its gaussian-blurred counter-part (Mean Top K and Blur Top K in the plot).\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d4a82003bd85c2a1\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"January 10, 2020\",\n      \"siteName\": \"distill.pub\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"efe5d316f1779dd5\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nOn the Evaluation Consistency of Attribution-based Explanations\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"efe5d316f1779dd5\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/html/2407.19471v1\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"58806523cc7d91f8\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTo this end, we assess the aforementioned eight attribution methods on all the generated test cases, i.e., with six models, four datasets and two ablation protocols (MoRF and LeRF). This yields a total of 26 groups of results, each corresponding to one test case. Some experimental results are presented in Figure 2.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"58806523cc7d91f8\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"July 28, 2024\",\n      \"siteName\": \"arxiv.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ab9e08bc7712ef6e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nModelship Attribution: Tracing Multi-Stage Manipulations Across Generative Models\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ab9e08bc7712ef6e\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/html/2506.02405\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"aa66903502146700\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nIn the ablation study, removing the Sequence Slice—i.e., directly feeding only the final M4 output to the transformer for Enhanced cross attention with ... italic_S start_POSTSUPERSCRIPT italic_t italic_o italic_k end_POSTSUPERSCRIPT—results in a notable drop in performance as Table 2 shows, suggesting that leveraging intermediate features is crucial for capturing fine-grained visual cues.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"aa66903502146700\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"June 3, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"arxiv.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9c7b12339a28aa86\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n[PDF] Ablation-CAM: Visual Explanations for Deep Convolutional Network via Gradient-free Localization | Semantic Scholar\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"9c7b12339a28aa86\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/Ablation-CAM:-Visual-Explanations-for-Deep-Network-Desai-Ramaswamy/9f5c43e85d2ae218f6082505dea8a5e980ed2f02\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8dbcdfa2ed6f6e47\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThis approach – Ablation-based Class Activation Mapping (Ablation CAM) <strong>uses ablation analysis to determine the importance of individual feature map units w.r.t.</strong> class to produce a coarse localization map highlighting the important regions ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8dbcdfa2ed6f6e47\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.semanticscholar.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c531a15e3b650879\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAblation Studies: XAI Methods for Tabular Data | Capital One\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c531a15e3b650879\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://capitalone.com/tech/machine-learning/xai-ablation-study\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"54fe71e9572a66d5\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe effect baselines have on post-hoc explanations can be easily seen in the image domain. Sturmfels et al. visualize attributions from Integrated Gradients (IG) using other reference images besides the usual black pixel baseline image. Varying baseline reference colors cause significant variation in the assigned attribution. Notice, in Figure 2, how the location of the high-intensity pixels from the attribution map change from the white input pixels to the black input pixels of the killer whale.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"54fe71e9572a66d5\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"January 20, 2023\",\n      \"siteName\": \"capitalone.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1f0ff29bd537dfbf\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nInterpretable Deep Learning Part II: Visual Interpretability with Attribution Methods\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1f0ff29bd537dfbf\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://metrics-lab.github.io/2020/10/08/visual-interpretability-with-attribution-methods.html\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2ef9dce7ea9b61bb\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nFeature attribution methods, or saliency methods, are <strong>one of the most popular local explanation methods for the interpretation of tasks of image classification or regression</strong>. These post-hoc techniques typically produce a heat-map showing how important each region or pixel of a particular picture ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2ef9dce7ea9b61bb\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"metrics-lab.github.io\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ba66916fedcf6df9\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAblation study on the effect of multimodal features. | Download Scientific Diagram\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"ba66916fedcf6df9\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.researchgate.net/figure/Ablation-study-on-the-effect-of-multimodal-features_tbl1_361762774\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"62c06d0f6a2e1fab\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThis study examines how various types of XAI explanations (<strong>confidence score, example-based method, and feature attribution</strong>) coupled with different decision-making sequences (one-way, parallel, and interactive) affect users’ trust and their ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"62c06d0f6a2e1fab\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.researchgate.net\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a5bf9c9414a98699\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n(PDF) Ablation Studies to Uncover Structure of Learned Representations in Artificial Neural Networks\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a5bf9c9414a98699\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/339541123_Ablation_Studies_to_Uncover_Structure_of_Learned_Representations_in_Artificial_Neural_Networks\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"03a7f1ced61cd33c\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nFor image captioning and VQA, our visualizations show that even non-attention based models learn to localize discriminative regions of input image. We devise a way to identify important neurons through Grad-CAM and combine it with neuron names (Bau et al. in Computer vision and pattern recognition, 2017) to provide textual explanations for model decisions. Finally, we design and conduct human studies to measure if Grad-CAM explanations help users establish appropriate trust in predictions from deep networks and show that Grad-CAM helps untrained users successfully discern a ‘stronger’ deep network from a ‘weaker’ one even when both make identical predictions.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"03a7f1ced61cd33c\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"February 27, 2020\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.researchgate.net\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"26dab9e90ca1b6c6\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nOn the Evaluation Consistency of Attribution-Based Explanations | Springer Nature Link\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"26dab9e90ca1b6c6\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-72897-6_12\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7e7de7c9da37d29a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nLNCS, vol. 12535, pp. 120–134. Springer, Cham (2020). https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-66415-2_8 ... Chattopadhay, A., Sarkar, A., Howlader, P., Balasubramanian, V.N.: Grad-cam++: generalized gradient-based visual explanations for deep convolutional networks.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7e7de7c9da37d29a\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"link.springer.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7a2355d22d31f327\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAblation-CAM: Visual Explanations for Deep Convolutional Network via\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7a2355d22d31f327\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content_WACV_2020/papers/Desai_Ablation-CAM_Visual_Explanations_for_Deep_Convolutional_Network_via_Gradient-free_Localization_WACV_2020_paper.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"50a0695a51ccf255\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n<strong>The ablation of unit k leads to a (possibly) reduced activa-</strong> ... Figure 3: Ablation CAM and Grad CAM visualizations are shown for two images.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"50a0695a51ccf255\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"openaccess.thecvf.com\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "Ablation Study of Attribution Methods for Visual Explanations 2020 figure 7", "provider": "brave", "count": 10, "tookMs": 2270, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"bd3a4c6153535210\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nVisualizing the Impact of Feature Attribution Baselines\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"bd3a4c6153535210\">>>", "url": "https://distill.pub/2020/attribution-baselines/", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d4a82003bd85c2a1\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n. At the heart of the issue is that we don’t have ground truth explanations: we are trying to evaluate which methods best explain our network without actually knowing what our networks are doing. One simple way to evaluate the importance scores that expected/integrated gradients produces is to see whether ablating the top k features as ranked by their importance decreases the predicted output logit. In the figure below, we ablate either by mean-imputation or by replacing each pixel by its gaussian-blurred counter-part (Mean Top K and Blur Top K in the plot).\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"d4a82003bd85c2a1\">>>", "published": "January 10, 2020", "siteName": "distill.pub"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"efe5d316f1779dd5\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nOn the Evaluation Consistency of Attribution-based Explanations\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"efe5d316f1779dd5\">>>", "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2407.19471v1", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"58806523cc7d91f8\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nTo this end, we assess the aforementioned eight attribution methods on all the generated test cases, i.e., with six models, four datasets and two ablation protocols (MoRF and LeRF). This yields a total of 26 groups of results, each corresponding to one test case. Some experimental results are presented in Figure 2.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"58806523cc7d91f8\">>>", "published": "July 28, 2024", "siteName": "arxiv.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ab9e08bc7712ef6e\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nModelship Attribution: Tracing Multi-Stage Manipulations Across Generative Models\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ab9e08bc7712ef6e\">>>", "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2506.02405", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"aa66903502146700\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nIn the ablation study, removing the Sequence Slice—i.e., directly feeding only the final M4 output to the transformer for Enhanced cross attention with ... italic_S start_POSTSUPERSCRIPT italic_t italic_o italic_k end_POSTSUPERSCRIPT—results in a notable drop in performance as Table 2 shows, suggesting that leveraging intermediate features is crucial for capturing fine-grained visual cues.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"aa66903502146700\">>>", "published": "June 3, 2025", "siteName": "arxiv.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9c7b12339a28aa86\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n[PDF] Ablation-CAM: Visual Explanations for Deep Convolutional Network via Gradient-free Localization | Semantic Scholar\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"9c7b12339a28aa86\">>>", "url": "https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/Ablation-CAM:-Visual-Explanations-for-Deep-Network-Desai-Ramaswamy/9f5c43e85d2ae218f6082505dea8a5e980ed2f02", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8dbcdfa2ed6f6e47\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThis approach – Ablation-based Class Activation Mapping (Ablation CAM) <strong>uses ablation analysis to determine the importance of individual feature map units w.r.t.</strong> class to produce a coarse localization map highlighting the important regions ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"8dbcdfa2ed6f6e47\">>>", "siteName": "www.semanticscholar.org"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c531a15e3b650879\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nAblation Studies: XAI Methods for Tabular Data | Capital One\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"c531a15e3b650879\">>>", "url": "https://capitalone.com/tech/machine-learning/xai-ablation-study", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"54fe71e9572a66d5\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe effect baselines have on post-hoc explanations can be easily seen in the image domain. Sturmfels et al. visualize attributions from Integrated Gradients (IG) using other reference images besides the usual black pixel baseline image. Varying baseline reference colors cause significant variation in the assigned attribution. Notice, in Figure 2, how the location of the high-intensity pixels from the attribution map change from the white input pixels to the black input pixels of the killer whale.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"54fe71e9572a66d5\">>>", "published": "January 20, 2023", "siteName": "capitalone.com"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1f0ff29bd537dfbf\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nInterpretable Deep Learning Part II: Visual Interpretability with Attribution Methods\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"1f0ff29bd537dfbf\">>>", "url": "https://metrics-lab.github.io/2020/10/08/visual-interpretability-with-attribution-methods.html", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2ef9dce7ea9b61bb\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nFeature attribution methods, or saliency methods, are <strong>one of the most popular local explanation methods for the interpretation of tasks of image classification or regression</strong>. These post-hoc techniques typically produce a heat-map showing how important each region or pixel of a particular picture ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"2ef9dce7ea9b61bb\">>>", "siteName": "metrics-lab.github.io"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ba66916fedcf6df9\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nAblation study on the effect of multimodal features. | Download Scientific Diagram\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"ba66916fedcf6df9\">>>", "url": "https://www.researchgate.net/figure/Ablation-study-on-the-effect-of-multimodal-features_tbl1_361762774", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"62c06d0f6a2e1fab\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThis study examines how various types of XAI explanations (<strong>confidence score, example-based method, and feature attribution</strong>) coupled with different decision-making sequences (one-way, parallel, and interactive) affect users’ trust and their ...\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"62c06d0f6a2e1fab\">>>", "siteName": "www.researchgate.net"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a5bf9c9414a98699\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n(PDF) Ablation Studies to Uncover Structure of Learned Representations in Artificial Neural Networks\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a5bf9c9414a98699\">>>", "url": "https://www.researchgate.net/publication/339541123_Ablation_Studies_to_Uncover_Structure_of_Learned_Representations_in_Artificial_Neural_Networks", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"03a7f1ced61cd33c\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nFor image captioning and VQA, our visualizations show that even non-attention based models learn to localize discriminative regions of input image. We devise a way to identify important neurons through Grad-CAM and combine it with neuron names (Bau et al. in Computer vision and pattern recognition, 2017) to provide textual explanations for model decisions. Finally, we design and conduct human studies to measure if Grad-CAM explanations help users establish appropriate trust in predictions from deep networks and show that Grad-CAM helps untrained users successfully discern a ‘stronger’ deep network from a ‘weaker’ one even when both make identical predictions.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"03a7f1ced61cd33c\">>>", "published": "February 27, 2020", "siteName": "www.researchgate.net"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"26dab9e90ca1b6c6\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nOn the Evaluation Consistency of Attribution-Based Explanations | Springer Nature Link\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"26dab9e90ca1b6c6\">>>", "url": "https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-72897-6_12", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"7e7de7c9da37d29a\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nLNCS, vol. 12535, pp. 120–134. Springer, Cham (2020). https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-66415-2_8 ... Chattopadhay, A., Sarkar, A., Howlader, P., Balasubramanian, V.N.: Grad-cam++: generalized gradient-based visual explanations for deep convolutional networks.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"7e7de7c9da37d29a\">>>", "siteName": "link.springer.com"}, {"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"7a2355d22d31f327\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nAblation-CAM: Visual Explanations for Deep Convolutional Network via\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"7a2355d22d31f327\">>>", "url": "https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content_WACV_2020/papers/Desai_Ablation-CAM_Visual_Explanations_for_Deep_Convolutional_Network_via_Gradient-free_Localization_WACV_2020_paper.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"50a0695a51ccf255\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\